"On Thu, 2002-08-22 at 19:10, Troy Engel wrote: > Anyone have an idea what the heck RedHat did here, and why we're now > trying to install a ton of crap I don't want? (I'm hoping someone else > has chased this down and could save me time... ;) ) I'm told that even our best people occasionally screw up. And QA had tested the rpm on an ""Everything"" install. Expect a fixed version soon, and QA procedures have been adjusted to catch this kind of braindamage in the future. There is nothing really wrong with the binary inside the rpm, so if you want to --nodeps for now it's ok. -- Chris Kloiber _______________________________________________ RPM-List mailing list <RPM-List@freshrpms.net> http://lists.freshrpms.net/mailman/listinfo/rpm-list",,ham
