much > government regulation are not saying that a state of nature (no private > replacements, no government regulation) is better than government > regulation itself. > > And in my experience people who label themselves 'Green' (which does not > include everyone who loves trees and thinks smokestacks are ugly) is a > watermelon. > > > > > > -----Original Message----- > > From: fork-admin@xent.com [mailto:fork-admin@xent.com] On Behalf Of > Geege > > Schuman > > > > funny. i read it as green = red, as in accounting, as in fiscally > > irresponsible. which do you think is the worse indictment - > > overregulation > > or overspending? there are many (dickheads) who buy into the > > neo-conservative media's (fox's) definiton of ""liberal"" as ""one who > seeks > > to > > impose both."" > > >",,ham
