">>>>> ""v"" == vernon <vernon@b2unow.com> writes: v> Some of my ""Security Violations"" and ""Unusual System Events"" are being v> tagged as SPAM by SpamAssassin. How do I get SA to ignore these messages? whitelists. you *really* have to white list any message source that discusses or is used to report spam, else the reports will be marked as spam, given that they have the spam indicators in them, usually... This is the *only* whitelisting I use. ------------------------------------------------------- This sf.net email is sponsored by:ThinkGeek Welcome to geek heaven. http://thinkgeek.com/sf _______________________________________________ Spamassassin-talk mailing list Spamassassin-talk@lists.sourceforge.net https://lists.sourceforge.net/lists/listinfo/spamassassin-talk",,ham
