"URL: http://boingboing.net/#85481626 Date: Not supplied DVDSynth is an open source project that allows you to splice in your own footage, alternate audio, subtitles, etc, to any DVD. This means that you can insert your own non-sucky subtitles, make and circulate edit-lists that make highlight reels for your favorite movies, etc, etc. It all amounts to a sweet tool for making the audience into the _former audience_, participants in entertainment. Of course, it's also illegal under the DMCA, since the tool also necessarily circumvents the copy-prevention in pre-recorded DVDs to accomplish its ends. Link[1] Discuss[2] (_via NTK[3]_) [1] http://www.roundelay.net/dvdsynth/prerelease.html [2] http://www.quicktopic.com/boing/H/ymptgyYcJan [3] http://www.ntk.net/",,ham
