"URL: http://boingboing.net/#85531557 Date: Not supplied Disney's themepark business is in deep trouble in the post-9/11 world. A war with Iraq could really kill 'em: While aggressively adding attractions, Disney boosted its profit by steadily raising admission prices. The strategy worked, helping deliver record profit for Disney year after year. ""The strategy was build, build, build. Every year there was something new,"" said David Koenig, a Disney historian and author. ""It was an astounding growth period.... Now they're overexposed.""... Theme park operating income for Disney this year is expected to fall 27% to $1.16 billion, said Prudential Securities analyst Katherine Styponias. By 2003, she said, the business could climb to $1.49 billion, depending on whether the U.S. goes to war with Iraq. Link[1] Discuss[2] [1] http://www.latimes.com/business/la-fi-disney6oct06,0,1287712.story?coll=la%2Dheadlines%2Dbusiness%2Dmanual [2] http://www.quicktopic.com/boing/H/iewxPJy39cF7",,ham
